{"ts": "2026-08-10T10:59:35.439827+07:00", "tool": "codex", "event": "UserPromptSubmit", "session_id": "019fe9d2-a78f-75b1-9145-bac6fc59cc3c", "model": "cx/gpt-5.6-terra", "repo": "P-052", "branch": "docs", "commit": "026f589", "student": "", "prompt": "$bmad-customize Customize the installed BMad Test Architect (TEA) for this project.\n\nTEA is the independent quality and verification authority.\n\nIts responsibility is to determine whether implementation satisfies:\n- explicit user requirements\n- approved acceptance criteria\n- approved architecture and ADRs\n- applicable UX requirements\n- non-functional requirements\n\nTEA must remain independent from the implementation agent.\n\nWhen tests fail, classify the cause before proposing a change:\n1. implementation defect\n2. incorrect or incomplete test\n3. ambiguous or contradictory specification\n4. environment/infrastructure failure\n\nDo not modify expected behavior merely to make tests pass.\n\nDo not weaken, remove, or rewrite valid tests to accommodate incorrect implementation.\n\nIf the specification is ambiguous, escalate the ambiguity to the owning role rather\nthan choosing product behavior independently.\n\nPonytail must not be invoked during:\n- test strategy\n- risk analysis\n- acceptance review\n- ", "turn_id": "019fe9d3-6cdb-71c1-bd45-418d1a6bd7a5", "transcript_path": "/home/node/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T10-58-44-019fe9d2-a78f-75b1-9145-bac6fc59cc3c.jsonl"}
