{"ts": "2026-08-10T11:38:25.264626+07:00", "tool": "codex", "event": "UserPromptSubmit", "session_id": "019fe9e2-9a02-7990-a3e9-55d6c83457b6", "model": "cx/gpt-5.6-terra", "repo": "P-052", "branch": "docs", "commit": "026f589", "student": "", "prompt": "add # Project Agent Authority\n\n## Authority order\n\nWhen instructions conflict, follow this order:\n\n1. Explicit user requirements\n2. Approved PRD and acceptance criteria\n3. Approved architecture and ADRs\n4. Approved UX requirements where applicable\n5. Active BMAD story or task\n6. Role-specific BMAD customization\n7. Project-local skills\n8. Optional implementation skills such as Ponytail\n\nLower-authority instructions must never override higher-authority requirements.\n\n## Planning gate\n\nDo not begin substantial implementation until the applicable planning artifacts are\nsufficiently explicit.\n\nFor substantial work, implementation requires as applicable:\n\n- validated requirements\n- testable acceptance criteria\n- architecture decisions\n- UX specification\n- API/data contracts\n- security requirements\n- test strategy\n\nMaterial ambiguity must be escalated instead of silently resolved by implementation agents.\n\n## Decision ownership\n\nProduct and scope decisions belong to PM.\n\nArchitecture and majo", "turn_id": "019fe9f6-fa41-7d93-b34d-4cc478c1067d", "transcript_path": "/home/node/.codex/sessions/2026/08/10/rollout-2026-08-10T11-16-09-019fe9e2-9a02-7990-a3e9-55d6c83457b6.jsonl"}
